Forager: trail attributes in the roads layer (dispatch 2026-09-28-495, RECORD -601)

Against protomaps/basemaps at ca93fc06efbaff1c5f069d06edbe5de18839c1c8 (tiles 4.15.2).
Applied with `git apply` from the repository root by map-build/bin/build-basemap-jar.sh.

Adds six keys, the OpenStreetMap values passed through as mapped, to roads-layer features for
highway=path, footway, track, bridleway and steps: sac_scale, trail_visibility, informal,
tracktype, surface, foot. They appear at every zoom the way appears (owner's ruling B). Absent
tags emit nothing. No existing attribute changes; access stays at zoom 15 as upstream emits it
(ruling A). The tests, placed at the end of class RoadsTest (RoadsTest.java also holds class
RoadsOvertureTest, after it), pin these, plus the existing kind, kind_detail and minimum zoom of
those ways.

Also (dispatch 2026-10-21-pi-23; owner: "Paths only (Recommended)", after "Match Topo exactly"):
highway=track enters the roads layer at z11 instead of 12, and highway=path at z12 instead of 13,
to match the app's topo map. Only the feature's first zoom moves (foragerMinZoom, passed to
setMinZoom alone): the min_zoom attribute and the sort key keep upstream's values, so label
priority does not change, and it only ever lowers the zoom, so a way on a US route relation keeps
upstream's earlier one and private or no-access ways stay at 15. Names keep their zoom
(minzoomName 14); footway, bridleway, steps, cycleway, pedestrian, sidewalk, crossing and corridor
keep theirs. Upstream's testHighways rows for track and path are edited to the new zooms, and
tests named foragerZoom* pin the change and what it leaves alone.

